  data: {
    LLM: 'Match suit or number with the top of the play pile, or play a Whot (wild) and name a suit. If you cannot or do not wish to play, draw one card from the stock; your turn then ends. First to empty hand wins the round.',
    Player: 'Match suit or number with the top of the play pile, or play a Whot (wild) and name a suit. If you cannot or do not wish to play, draw one card from the stock; your turn then ends. First to empty hand wins the round.',
    objective: 'Be the first to get rid of all your cards; in multi-round play, avoid accumulating 100 or more penalty points.',
    gameplay: 'Match suit or number with the top of the play pile, or play a Whot (wild) and name a suit. If you cannot or do not wish to play, draw one card from the stock; your turn then ends. First to empty hand wins the round.',
    keyRules: [
      "Play a card matching the previous card's suit or number, or any Whot card (then name a suit).",
      'If unable or unwilling to play, draw one card from the stock; you may not play after drawing this turn.',
      'When the stock is exhausted, shuffle all but the top card of the play pile to form a new stock.',
      'Penalty scoring: circles, crosses, squares, triangles at face value; stars count double; Whot cards count 20. Players with 100 or more drop out; last remaining wins.',
