      players: 'Two or more players.',
      deck: 'A special Whot pack of 54 or 53 cards: five symbol suits (circle, triangle, cross, square, star) with uneven card counts per suit, plus four or five wild Whot cards (numbered 20). British packs from around 1990 often have four Whots (53 cards); earlier and Nigerian packs have five (54 cards).',
      equipment: 'Whot cards',
      dealing: 'Dealer deals six cards to each player one at a time; remainder forms the draw pile. First dealer is chosen by cutting the pack (lowest card deals, Whot counting 20).',
